      "side": 1,
      "message": "Thanks for review, on the source side, the values these are populated from are lifetime: they are aggregate ECC error counts, stored in non-volatile ROM and accumulated over the lifetime of the device — monotonically increasing.\n\nThat said, I agree the PDI itself doesn\u0027t make that guarantee explicit today, so the mapping currently relies on that implicit knowledge.\n\nWould you prefer I submit a phosphor-dbus-interfaces patch to make it explicit — e.g. add a boolean (something like isLifetime) so a consumer can distinguish lifetime counts from volatile ones? bmcweb would then only map to CacheMetricsTotal.LifeTime when that flag is set, turning the semantic from an assumption into a contract. Happy to go that route if you think it\u0027s the right call.Thanks.",
